{"name":"Notebook Paper","hex":"#e8ebe6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"notebook","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A book (physical or digital) in which notes or memoranda are written.","A kind of user interface in literate programming, allowing calculations to be interspersed with human-readable comments, diagrams, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/notebook"},{"term":"paper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sheet material typically used for writing on or printing on (or as a non-waterproof container), usually made by draining cellulose fibres from a suspension in water.","Ellipsis of newspaper; anything used as such (such as a newsletter or listing magazine)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of paper.","Insubstantial (from the weakness of common paper)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Notebook Paper","blocks":[{"text":"Notebook Paper is the debut studio album by American rapper Huey. It was released on June 19, 2007, via Hitz Committee/Jive/Zomba Records. Production was handled by several record producers, including Jazze Pha, StarGate, T-Mix and T-Pain. It features guest appearances from Asia Cruise, Diamond, Kydd Trell, Bow Wow, Lloyd, MeMpHiTz, T-Pain, Trey Songz and Yo Gotti."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/00/HueyNotebookPaper.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Notebook_Paper","wikidata":"Q16959105"},{"title":"Notebook","blocks":[{"text":"A notebook is a book or stack of paper pages that are often ruled and used for purposes such as note-taking, journaling, or other writing, drawing, or scrapbooking and more."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Notebooks.jpg/330px-Notebooks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Notebook","wikidata":"Q43013"},{"title":"Paper","blocks":[{"text":"Paper is a thin sheet of matted cellulose fibers. Largely derived from lignocellulose, paper is created from a pulp dissolved into a slurry that is drained and dried into sheets. Different types of paper are defined by constituent fiber, paper pulp, sizing, coating, paper size, paper density and grammage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Various_products_made_from_paper.JPG/330px-Various_products_made_from_paper.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paper","wikidata":"Q11472"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Legal_pad_and_pencil.jpg/500px-Legal_pad_and_pencil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Legal_pad_and_pencil.jpg/1280px-Legal_pad_and_pencil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Legal_pad_and_pencil.jpg/500px-Legal_pad_and_pencil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Legal pad and pencil","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALegal_pad_and_pencil.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Notebooks-rainbow.jpg/500px-Notebooks-rainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Notebooks-rainbow.jpg/1280px-Notebooks-rainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Notebooks-rainbow.jpg/500px-Notebooks-rainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Notebooks with different color covers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANotebooks-